{"name":"Black Rock","hex":"#2c2d3c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Rock","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The CBS Building in New York City.","A coastal area of Brighton, city of Brighton and Hove district, East Sussex, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Rock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Rock, South Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Black Rock is a hamlet in South Australia on the Black Rock Plains at the intersection of the south–north RM Williams Way (B80) between Jamestown and Orroroo and the west–east Wilmington–Ucolta Road (B56) to Peterborough, in the Mid North section of the state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Black_Rock_sign.jpg/330px-Black_Rock_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Rock%2C_South_Australia"},{"title":"Black Rock, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Black Rock is a suburb in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, 18 km south-east of Melbourne's Central Business District, located within the City of Bayside local government area. Black Rock recorded a population of 6,389 at the 2021 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Black_Rock_Victoria_b.jpg/330px-Black_Rock_Victoria_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Rock%2C_Victoria"},{"title":"Black Rock (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Rock is a 2012 American horror-thriller film directed by Katie Aselton, with a screenplay by her husband Mark Duplass. The film premiered on January 21, 2012 at the 2012 Sundance Film Festival and was released theatrically on May 17, 2013. Black Rock stars Aselton, Lake Bell, and Kate Bosworth as three friends who reunite after years apart on a remote island but end up having to fight for their lives."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/BlackRock2012TheatricalPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Rock_(2012_film)"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg/120px-Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg/250px-Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg/120px-Aerial_perspective_of_Black_Rock%2C_facing_south_along_Port_Philip_Bay._Jan_2019_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o